note draft
# Checked spec, not compiled code — see ../head/mine.tree's note. The real reader is ./code.tree's
# read-otf-loca-table, proven by deck/feed/test/otf-loca.tree. `short-format` comes from `head`'s own
# `index-to-loc-format` (0 = short, 1 = long) — resolved by whatever reads `loca` after `head`, not carried here,
# same single-responsibility split every other table in this package keeps. `mine case` here branches on a plain
# boolean, so the real reader uses `fork test`/a bare read instead (the same open notation question cmap's own
# mine.tree flags for a numeric branch — `feedback_term_fork_case_needs_form`, memory). The short entry's real
# value is the stored `ushort` doubled back into a byte offset (`code.tree`'s `multiply(..., code 2)`) — real
# processing beyond a raw field extraction, the same open "does the spec notation need a dedicated word" question
# gzip's own `mine.tree` already leaves unresolved for its trailer-length arithmetic.

mine loca-table
  take num-glyphs, like number
  take short-format, like boolean

  mine list
    bind count, call add(read num-glyphs, code 1)
    mine case, read short-format
      case true
        mine int
          bind width, code 2
          bind order, term big
          bind sign, term unsigned
      case false
        mine int
          bind width, code 4
          bind order, term big
          bind sign, term unsigned
    send offsets
